{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you today. I see you came in because of pain when swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been really sharp when I swallow. It’s dull most of the time, but then it spikes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned it started after your last admission. Any fever, chills, or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or breathing issues. I can talk and eat soft foods, but it hurts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, good. Your vitals are stable. We checked your blood — your hemoglobin is a bit low, but that’s been known. No signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve had anemia for a while. But this pain is new. And I feel a little dizzy — usually happens when I don’t drink enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. You were a bit lightheaded on arrival, so we gave you IV fluids. That should help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. Can I get some IV pain medicine? The Dilaudid works better than the oral ones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with IV Dilaudid for now to get your pain under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I also want to make sure I can have regular food. I’d like cookies — I’ve been eating soft stuff but I miss normal food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on regular diet. You’re able to eat and swallow safely, so no restrictions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My trach tube is okay, right? It hasn’t moved or anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked the chest X-ray — your trach tube is in the right place. No changes. Your lungs look clear too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried something was wrong down there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "ENT and pulmonology looked at you in the ER. They did a scope through your trach tube to check your airway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. Did they see anything? Infection? Swelling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No infection or swelling. Your vocal cords are moving fine, no pus or redness. But they did see some crusting in the airway — that could be contributing to the discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Crusting? Is that normal for me?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common with chronic trach use, especially with your history. We’ll keep you on your usual inhaled saline to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. So this pain isn’t from an infection or a problem with my surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it doesn’t look like it. The pain seems to be from irritation at the tracheal revision site, not an infection or structural issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s the plan? Just keep taking pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. We’ll control the pain with IV Dilaudid, then switch you to oral meds as you improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope the oral ones work. Last time, they didn’t help as much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use a combination — liquid Dilaudid, acetaminophen, and naproxen. That usually works better than one alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what about the dizziness? Is that just from not drinking enough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it looks like mild dehydration from reduced intake due to pain. The IV fluids should help. We’ll encourage you to drink more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll try. But it’s hard when swallowing hurts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2166-09-18 16:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. That’s why we’re focusing on pain control first — so you can eat and drink more comfortably."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your pain is better today, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, much better. I had some soup and even a cookie. Still a little sore, but manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to switch you to oral pain meds now — liquid naproxen, acetaminophen, and liquid Dilaudid as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the viscous lidocaine? Can I use that before meals?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. Use 15 mL of viscous lidocaine before meals to numb the area. It should help with swallowing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. So I’m going home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if everything stays on track. Your vitals are stable, you’re walking fine, and your pain is controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about follow-up? Should I see ENT or my pulmonologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please follow up with your PCP, pulmonologist, and ENT as scheduled. They’ll keep monitoring your airway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I should keep working on eating even if it’s a little uncomfortable?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The more you use it, the better it gets. The pain should continue to improve over the next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Doctor. I feel a lot better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2166-09-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Take care, and call if anything worsens."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2166-09-18 15:51:00",
    "admission_end": "2166-09-19 17:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of tracheobronchomalacia, tracheostomy, and multiple airway reconstructions was admitted for pain when swallowing, which she described as dull at baseline and sharp with swallowing. She had recently been hospitalized for pain and fluid resuscitation with a negative infectious workup. On admission, she was mildly lightheaded due to poor oral intake, which resolved with IV fluids. Evaluation by ENT and interventional pulmonology, including fiberoptic exam, showed no infection or structural abnormality but noted marked crusting in the airway. Pain was initially managed with IV hydromorphone and transitioned to oral hydromorphone, acetaminophen, naproxen, and viscous lidocaine. She tolerated a regular diet, pain improved, and she was discharged home with a one-week course of oral pain medications and instructions to follow up with her PCP, pulmonologist, and ENT.",
    "problems": [
      "Throat pain",
      "Dehydration",
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Other diseases of trachea and bronchus",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Chronic obstructive asthma, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
